rten entre 24 adjudicatarios distintos. El contrato [1], de 14.539,26 euros, se adjudicó en diciembre de 2025.\nQué no pueden demostrar: El hecho de que muchos contratos estén cerca del límite no indica que haya sido evadido el límite o que haya habido irregularidades. Puede deberse a razones legítimas como la necesidad de contratar en un momento específico o a precios de mercado.\nQué se puede revisar: Es necesario comprobar si los contratos [1], [2] y [3] atienden la misma necesidad. También se debe revisar si el adjudicatario A repite contratos en distintas áreas o si hubo ajustes en los presupuestos al final del año.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 33 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 9.6 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 3.4, with a 95% confidence interval of 2.1 to 5.5. December accounts for 21% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 13% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 3. Contract [1], for 14,539.26 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December and the high number of awardees do not prove improper actions. These could reflect market conditions or budget constraints, not wrongdoing.\nWhat can be checked: Check the December contracts for repeated purchases and verify if the same awardee was used for multiple needs. Review the distribution of contracts across different sectors to identify patterns.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["RC1ES22a9k25HQrHoP3G5A%3D%3D","B0OxET9dASRSYrkJkLlFdw%3D%3D","PbLyY9zcVZYeC9GJQOEBkQ%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-16"}}